From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolf Brokmann <rbrok@rolfbrokmann.de>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:14:08 +0100
Subject: drivers: net: ethernet: mediatek: disable ASP FSM parity

At 1 Gbps link speeds (125 MHz DDR RGMII), the Synopsys Automotive Safety
Package (ASP) in the MediaTek DWMAC5 triggers false uncorrectable
'FSMPES: FSM State Parity Error' interrupts on the MT8395 (Genio 1200 /
Radxa NIO 12L).

This leads to continuous adapter reset loops ('Reset adapter') and eventual
kernel soft lockups.

Intel's DWMAC driver (dwmac-intel.c) disables this FSM parity feature
(prtyen = 0) across multiple platforms for the same reason. Disabling the
FSM state parity check resolves the issue completely on my Radxa NIO 12L,
yielding a rock-solid 1 Gbps link (verified at 943 Mbit/s net TCP throughput
with 0 retransmissions via iperf3).

Assisted-by: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Rolf Brokmann <rbrok@rolfbrokmann.de>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-mediatek.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-mediatek.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-mediatek.c
index 30ae0dba7fff..09236f55c554 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-mediatek.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-mediatek.c
@@ -582,11 +582,11 @@ static int mediatek_dwmac_common_data(struct platform_device *pdev,
 	plat->safety_feat_cfg->mestee = 1;
 	plat->safety_feat_cfg->mrxee = 1;
 	plat->safety_feat_cfg->mtxee = 1;
 	plat->safety_feat_cfg->epsi = 0;
 	plat->safety_feat_cfg->edpp = 1;
-	plat->safety_feat_cfg->prtyen = 1;
+	plat->safety_feat_cfg->prtyen = 0;
 	plat->safety_feat_cfg->tmouten = 1;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < plat->tx_queues_to_use; i++) {
 		/* Default TX Q0 to use TSO and rest TXQ for TBS */
 		if (i > 0)
